Character Taste Observatory Design Skill

This project-specific Codex skill was created for Character Taste Lab
(character_taste_analyzer). It was informed by the design workflow and skill
structure of the following Apache-2.0-licensed works:

1. `frontend-design` by Anthropic <support@anthropic.com>
   Project reference: anthropics/frontend-design
   Upstream learning reference:
   https://github.com/anthropics/claude-cookbooks/blob/main/coding/prompting_for_frontend_aesthetics.ipynb

2. `frontend-design-codex` from KilimiaoSix/agent-skills
   https://github.com/KilimiaoSix/agent-skills/tree/main/skills/frontend-design-codex
   This work is itself a Codex-native adaptation of Anthropic's public
   `frontend-design` workflow.

The present skill substantially customizes those general frontend-design ideas
into a self-contained visual system, page grammar, implementation workflow,
and browser-verification checklist for a "dedicated astronomical instrument
for observing character preferences." It does not require either referenced
skill at runtime.

The names Anthropic, Claude, OpenAI, and Codex are used only to describe origin
and compatibility. This project does not claim affiliation or endorsement.
